---
title: "User path: install, use, troubleshoot (0 → 5 is the order)"
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph ROW1["User path · strictly 0 → 5; red = must do, amber = the places people trip on"]
    direction LR
    subgraph T0["0 · Precheck"]
      direction TB
      T0a["node -v ≥ 18<br/>git --version works"]
      T0b["run at the repo root<br/>(where .git lives)"]
      T0c["Windows / macOS / Linux all fine"]
    end
    subgraph T1["1 · Install"]
      direction TB
      T1a["npm i -g dsh-signoff"]
      T1b["no global install: npx dsh-signoff p1 once"]
      T1c["behind a corporate proxy set npm proxy<br/>or npx cannot fetch the package"]
    end
    subgraph T2["2 · Init"]
      direction TB
      T2a["signoff init"]
      T2b["repo already has husky hooks: add --chain<br/>otherwise yours get replaced"]
      T2c["test command differs per machine: --lock-test"]
      T2d["see what it will write: --dry-run"]
      T2e["leave CI alone: --no-ci"]
    end
    subgraph T3["3 · Daily commits"]
      direction TB
      T3a["git commit<br/>pre-commit runs the five gates"]
      T3b["marker and trailer written only when all five pass"]
      T3c["status: what got installed<br/>doctor: why it does nothing"]
      T3d["explain p2: how this gate decides"]
      T3e["audit --since-install: who really passed"]
    end
    subgraph T4["4 · Red? check in this order"]
      direction TB
      T4a["doctor: are the hooks running at all"]
      T4b["not running → init --chain"]
      T4c["tests really fail → fix code, not thresholds"]
      T4d["coverage short → add assertions, or --strict for the stricter verdict"]
      T4e["queue incomplete → finish the card"]
      T4f["ledger broken / trailer missing → p4 ask/confirm or roll back"]
      T4g["P5 false positive → rewrite the wording, not the word list"]
    end
    subgraph T5["5 · Upgrade and uninstall"]
      direction TB
      T5a["upgrade: npm i -g dsh-signoff@latest<br/>then signoff init to refresh the hooks"]
      T5b["uninstall default: remove hooks, keep config"]
      T5c["--keep-config / --all: two more thorough levels"]
    end
    T0 --> T1 --> T2 --> T3 --> T4 --> T5
  end

  subgraph ROW2["The three real-world dimensions · they do not change your flow, they change what you see"]
    direction LR
    subgraph PL["Platform differences"]
      direction TB
      PL1["Windows: hooks launch through .ps1 / .cmd<br/>exec bit irrelevant; a GBK console mangles Chinese output"]
      PL2["macOS / Linux: hooks need the exec bit<br/>init sets it, doctor --fix repairs it"]
      PL3["containers / CI: often no user.name or user.email<br/>the commit fails and it is unrelated to the gates"]
      PL4["SMB / NFS: lock atomicity cannot be proven<br/>mkdir beats O_EXCL, still best effort"]
    end
    subgraph EN["Environment differences"]
      direction TB
      EN1["Node 18 / 20 / 22 / 26 all tested in CI"]
      EN2["shallow clone: audit baseline unreachable → red<br/>CI needs fetch-depth 0"]
      EN3["monorepo: the repo root is the unit<br/>per-package init creates two hook sets"]
      EN4["repo without tests: reports 'no test command detected'<br/>it never fakes a pass"]
      EN5["works offline: the gates never touch the network<br/>only npx needs it"]
    end
    subgraph RED["Red lines · do not"]
      direction TB
      RD1["--no-verify → the audit shows missing"]
      RD2["SIGNOFF_SKIP=1 → the marker records skip"]
      RD3["loosening thresholds to turn red green = deleting the evidence"]
    end
  end

  PL ~~~ EN ~~~ RED

  ROW1 -->|same verdicts, different symptoms| ROW2

